    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Burning on passing urine and needing to go often for two days, at 24 weeks. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mumtaz Mahal is a 37-year-old woman in her fourteenth pregnancy, at 24 weeks 2 days by a 13-week dating scan, who came in the same day with two days of burning when she passes urine, frequency, and urgency, with a little lower abdominal discomfort. She has had no fever, chills, back or flank pain, nausea, or vomiting. She has had no tightenings or period-like pains, no fluid leaking, and no bleeding, and the baby is moving well. She has been drinking less than usual on a long road journey last week. The urine culture at her first visit grew nothing. She takes folic acid and aspirin 81 mg, and had her second dose of intravenous iron three weeks ago. She has no allergies. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Two days</td></tr><tr><td>Symptoms</td><td>Dysuria, frequency, urgency, mild suprapubic discomfort</td></tr><tr><td>Pertinent negatives</td><td>No fever, chills, flank pain, vomiting, contractions, leaking fluid, or bleeding</td></tr><tr><td>Fetal movement</td><td>Normal</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Drinking less during a long road journey last week; intake urine culture negative</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

